    "narrative": "The offensive outlook for Ghost Ride the WHIP on July 3rd centers on high-upside matchups against mediocre arms, led by **Mickey Moniak**, who boasts our highest daily score (75.33). His projection is heavily buoyed by an exceptional 14% park factor and a favorable platoon advantage against Logan Webb. **Brice Turang** (73.74) and **James Wood** (73.57) are our other primary pillars today; **Brice Turang** benefits from a strong spot in the three-hole, while **James Wood** brings elite xwOBA metrics (0.418) into a favorable encounter with a pitcher sporting a 4.60 xERA. While **Corbin Carroll** is a roster staple, his 52.12 score reflects the difficulty of facing a sub-3.00 xERA arm in Kyle Harrison, highlighting the premium we are placing on efficiency over name value in today's set.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision landed on **Edwin Arroyo**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 50.06 score. While his switch-hitting profile and favorable park context were appealing, he was ultimately outpaced by the higher floor provided by our middle-order anchors. We are also keeping a close eye on **Travis Bazzana**, whose 51.97 score is currently threatened by a 38% rain risk. Should the weather turn, we have depth ready to pivot to ensure we don't squander a game cap on a washout. Additionally, while **Josh Naylor** (45.59) was considered, the optimizer shied away due to a difficult matchup against Dylan Cease, whose elite SP metrics (3.01 xERA) suppressed **Josh Naylor**\u2019s ceiling, reinforcing our commitment to avoiding low-efficiency starts that don't contribute significantly to our pursuit of stolen bases or batting average.",
